# Where the row of a call on numbers, with its rule of ranges, leaves one integer, the walk gives that integer and builds no record (constantWhereRowLeavesOneIntegerInNumberBuiltins()). THE LIE: the row writes its least integer alone.
# No record, no check: "least" for "more", no stop, UNDER THE OPTION TOO, for Math.abs, ceil, floor, max, min, round, sign and trunc. Under the word the short way is not taken: the code in line is built and held against its row.
